course: dictionary
lesson: 4808
title: Hump: a lump, a bump, and a grumpy mood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Hump» is one of those words. You can find out which meaning fits by reading the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «A camel's hump stores fat, not water, which gives energy when food is short.» Here a hump is a round lump on a camel's back. The words stores fat and food tell you that.
explain: «Dad has the hump because the bus was late.» Dad is not carrying a lump. Have the hump means he is grumpy. Try the meaning in the sentence: Dad is grumpy because the bus was late. It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Hump can also be a verb, which is an action word. Informal speech uses it to mean carry something heavy: «He humped the boxes up the stairs.» Check the context before you choose a meaning.
fact: A hump is a round lump that sticks up, such as on a camel's back.
fact: A speed hump is a raised bump across a road that slows cars down, often near schools.
fact: «Over the hump» means past the hardest part of a job.
fact: «Have the hump» (British) means to be grumpy.
fact: Camels store fat in their humps, not water. A thirsty camel can drink about 100 litres in about ten minutes.
fact: «Hump day» is a name for Wednesday, the middle of the week.
exercise: «A camel's hump stores fat, not water.» What is a camel's hump? | A pond full of water | A bag for carrying food | A kind of tent | *A round lump on its back
exercise: Speed humps slow cars near schools. What is a speed hump? | A wide, flat path for bikes | *A raised bump across the road | A sign that says stop | A big puddle in the road
exercise: Sam says, «I'm over the hump with my maths homework.» What does over the hump mean? | He has climbed a real hill | He is grumpy about it | *He has got past the hardest part | He has finished every question and gone home
test: «Wednesday is hump day, the middle of the week.» What does hump day mean? | A day for carrying heavy boxes | The day the bus is late | Saturday, the day of football | *Wednesday, the middle of the week
test: «Dad has the hump because the bus was late.» What does have the hump mean? | Is laughing loudly | *Is grumpy | Has a bump on his back | Is climbing a hill
exam: «A camel's hump stores fat, not water, which gives energy when food is short.» Which is true? | It holds milk for the calves | It stores water for the desert | It is made of sand and stone | *It stores fat, which gives energy when food is short
